Features/Characteristics of Debentures
Borrowed Fund: Debentures are part of borrowed
fund capital as debenture holders are considered
as the creditors of the company.
Fixed Rate of Interest: The interest on debentures
is paid at a fixed rate. The rate of interest is
decided in the annual general meeting of the
company.
