Features/Characteristics of Debentures
Compulsory Payment of Interest: Payment of
regular and fixed rate of interest is a legal
obligation of the company. Company has to pay
interest to its debenture holders irrespective of
its profit-earning capacity.
Appointment of Trustee: When a large number of
debentures are sold to the general public then
usually a trustee is appointed. The trustee is
appointed to ensure that the borrowing firm fulfils
its contractual obligations.
